  "worked_solution": "The notation \n\n$$\nf:[-1,1]\\to R\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $f$ maps the set $[-1,1]$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $[-1,1],$ and\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $R.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
